# TS-027 bounded scratch investigation (informal; not a test result), 2026-11-03 18:36-18:50 IST.
# Baseline: be788ca, working tree clean; amr_ws unchanged; scratch only (<scratch> = a temporary scratch folder). gz-sim 8.15.0, gz-physics 7.8.0, gz_ros2_control 1.2.20.
# Scripts: TS-027_fixture_exp.py (gz.sim8 TestFixture, no ROS), TS-027_launch_probe.py + TS-027_run_launch.sh (real sim.launch.py),
#          TS-027_gz_jc_probe.py + TS-027_run_gz.sh (real gz sim server, runtime spawn, gz JointController), and the Task D procedure (C1/C2).
# Models: amr_s.sdf = xacro use_sensors:=true (no use_ros2_control: no M2 contact surfaces, cylinder wheels);
#         amr_full_noctl.sdf = the launch expansion (use_ros2_control:=true use_sensors:=true) with only the gz_ros2_control <plugin> removed;
#         amr_jc.sdf = amr_full_noctl.sdf + two gz-sim JointController plugins (velocity mode = JointVelocityCmd).
# Columns (fixture): true accel = (v(t1)-v(t0))/(t1-t0) from the ground-truth link velocity; physics-reported = mean of the
#   per-step WorldLinearAcceleration component (the engine frame data the IMU also uses); IMU = mean of /imu linear_acceleration.

## Source reading (gz-sim8 Imu.cc, Physics.cc; gz-physics7 dartsim KinematicsFeatures.cc; gz_ros2_control jazzy gz_system.cpp)
# IMU system copies the LinearAcceleration component of the IMU entity into gz-sensors ImuSensor (which subtracts gravity).
# Physics::UpdateSim fills that component from the engine frame data at the sensor offset (LinkFrameDataAtOffset), rotated to the body frame.
# dartsim FrameDataRelativeToWorld: linearAcceleration = frame->getLinearAcceleration() (instantaneous, this step).
# gz_ros2_control does not touch IMU components; it writes JointVelocityCmd only in write(), i.e. once per controller_manager cycle.

